    "summary": "Architecture overview, design philosophy, and quickstart guide for MotionFoundry v2.0.",
    "body": "MotionFoundry v2.0 is a production-ready, open-source animated React component ecosystem engineered for modern React 19 and Next.js App Router applications. All 48 components — the 24-piece **Core** collection and the 24-piece **Studio Kit** collection — are built with strict TypeScript interfaces, scoped CSS Modules, hardware-accelerated Motion (`motion/react`), SVG, or HTML5 Canvas engines tailored to each animation, and automatic `prefers-reduced-motion` accessibility support.\n\n### Architectural Pillars\n\n- **Multi-Engine Animation Architecture**: Uses `motion/react` for spring physics and shared-layout choreography (`KineticType`, `TextMorph`, `MagneticButton`, `ElasticPressButton`, `HoloTiltCard`, `PortalRevealPanel`, `MagneticDock`, `MorphingCommandPalette`), pure CSS & SVG filters for zero-runtime continuous effects (`OrbitingWords`, `VelocityButton`, `LiquidGlassCard`, `MorphingBorder`, `InfiniteMarquee`, `FluidMeshBackground`, `NoiseAurora`, `LiquidBlob`), and capped HTML5 Canvas loops for spatial node networks (`ConstellationCard`, `OrbitingParticles`).\n- **Two Collections**: Core covers spatial surfaces, canvas networks, and kinetic typography; [Studio Kit](/docs/studio-kit) covers everyday product motion — text reveals, feedback buttons, interactive cards, ambient backgrounds, loaders, and list interactions.\n- **Single Source of Truth Registry**: Every component's `.tsx` and `.module.css` implementation inside `packages/ui/src/` feeds the shared `registry/registry.json` manifest (generated by `node scripts/build-registry.mjs`), the `@motionfoundry/ui` package build, the `motionfoundry` CLI installer, and the interactive code tabs on this website.\n- **Configurable Brand Identity**: The working brand name (`MotionFoundry`) and package scope (`@motionfoundry/ui`) are centralized in `apps/docs/lib/brand.ts` so teams can fork and rebrand the entire ecosystem by editing a single file.",
    "code": "// Central brand configuration (apps/docs/lib/brand.ts)\nexport const BRAND_CONFIG = {\n  name: \"MotionFoundry\",\n  packageScope: \"@motionfoundry/ui\",\n  cliCommand: \"motionfoundry\",\n  version: \"2.0.0\",\n  license: \"MIT\",\n};"
