    "category": "Overview",
    "summary": "Choose between the CLI source installer, workspace/npm package imports, or direct copy-and-paste.",
    "body": "MotionFoundry supports three first-class distribution workflows depending on whether you want full ownership of the component source files in your repository or a versioned package dependency.\n\n### Workflow A — CLI Source Installation (Recommended)\n\nRun the `motionfoundry` CLI to copy selected components and their scoped `.module.css` files directly into your project's `components/ui/` directory (stylesheets land in `components/styles/`, matching each component's `../styles/<slug>.module.css` import):\n\n- Detects Next.js App Router (`src/app` or `app`), Next.js Pages Router, or Vite/React projects automatically.\n- Checks for existing files before writing and preserves your custom edits unless `--overwrite` is passed.\n- Prints exact peer dependencies (`motion`) required by the selected components.\n- Filter the catalog by collection with `npx motionfoundry list --collection studio-kit`.\n\n### Workflow B — Package Imports (`@motionfoundry/ui`)\n\nInside a pnpm monorepo workspace (or once published to an npm registry), install `@motionfoundry/ui` alongside `motion` and import named components directly. Note: in this repository, `@motionfoundry/ui` is configured as a local workspace package (`workspace:*`) ready for `npm publish`.\n\n### Workflow C — Direct Copy and Paste\n\nOpen any of the 48 component detail pages, switch to the **Component** and **CSS Module** tabs, and click **Copy** to drop the standalone `.tsx` and `.module.css` files into your codebase.",
