    "body": "MotionFoundry ships 11 brand design systems as **DESIGN.md** files: Vercel, Cursor, Claude, Framer, Apple, Airbnb, Expo, ElevenLabs, Runway, Resend, and Spotify. A DESIGN.md is a plain-text design system — color tokens, type ramp, radii, component specs, and do's and don'ts — written so both people and AI coding agents can follow it. Browse them on the [Design Systems](/designs) page.\n\n### Where they live\n\n- `design-md/<id>/DESIGN.md` — the vendored files, unchanged from [VoltAgent/awesome-design-md](https://github.com/VoltAgent/awesome-design-md) (MIT, see `design-md/LICENSE`).\n- `design-md/themes.json` — a curated MotionFoundry theme per brand: canvas, surfaces, text, borders, accent, radius, and font stacks, picked from each file's tokens.\n- `registry/designs.json` — generated by `node scripts/build-designs.mjs`, which parses both DESIGN.md formats (YAML frontmatter tokens, or prose color bullets plus a type hierarchy table).\n\n### Theming components\n\nEvery component CSS Module reads its palette from CSS custom properties with the original value as the fallback, for example `background: var(--mf-surface, #141419)`. Nothing changes until you set a variable, and setting them on any wrapper re-skins everything inside it:\n\n- `--mf-bg` and `--mf-fg` — page background and primary text (solid buttons invert these).\n- `--mf-surface`, `--mf-surface-raised` — cards, inputs, and raised layers.\n- `--mf-muted`, `--mf-subtle` — secondary and tertiary text.\n- `--mf-border`, `--mf-border-strong` — hairlines and hover borders.\n- `--mf-accent` — the default accent; color props such as `accentColor` still win when passed.\n\n### Using a preset\n\nOn any component page, open the **Design** picker above the preview to apply a brand: the stage switches to the brand canvas and every color control is recolored from its palette. Each design page also shows a token-built landing sketch, live components, swatches, a type specimen, and copy-ready CSS.\n\n### Adding another design system\n\n1. Copy `design-md/<id>/DESIGN.md` from awesome-design-md (or write your own in the same format).\n2. Add an entry to `design-md/themes.json` with the `theme` fields — `accent` and `secondary` must be `#rrggbb` hex values.\n3. Run `node scripts/build-designs.mjs`; the gallery, sidebar, search, and component Design pickers pick it up automatically.",
    "code": "# regenerate registry/designs.json after editing design-md/\nnode scripts/build-designs.mjs\n\n# CI verifies it is up to date\nnode scripts/build-designs.mjs --check"
