    "slug": "troubleshooting",
    "title": "Troubleshooting",
    "category": "Quality & Standards",
    "summary": "Resolving common issues with Next.js Server Components, motion/react imports, and CSS Module bundlers.",
    "body": "### Common Questions & Fixes\n\n- **Error: `import { motion } from \"framer-motion\"` is deprecated**: MotionFoundry uses the modern `motion` package (`v14+`) and imports strictly from `\"motion/react\"`. Run `pnpm add motion` rather than `framer-motion`.\n- **Styles appear unstyled when using `@motionfoundry/ui`**: Ensure you have imported `@motionfoundry/ui/styles.css` in your root `app/layout.tsx`.\n- **CLI reports `Conflict detected: file already exists`**: The CLI protects your existing source code by default. Pass `--overwrite` (`npx motionfoundry add kinetic-type --overwrite`) to replace the file with the upstream registry version.",
